# Code Review

When reviewing code, check:

## Correctness
- Does the code match the spec? Check each acceptance criterion.
- Are edge cases from the spec handled?
- Are external data sources validated? (null checks, type guards at system boundaries)
- Is error handling present? (API endpoints catch errors, frontend handles fetch failures)

## Framework conventions
- Does the code follow patterns established in `AGENTS.md` and the project?
- Are there SSR/hydration safety issues? (browser-only APIs in render path)

## Code quality
- No `any` types (TypeScript) — use `unknown` + type guards for external data
- No premature abstraction — three similar lines beat a wrapper used once
- No speculative features beyond the spec
- No commented-out code — git preserves history
- Comments explain *why*, never *what*

## Report format
- **[critical]** `file:line` — must fix before commit
- **[warning]** `file:line` — should fix, potential issue
- **[nit]** `file:line` — minor suggestion
